    cuesEn: "1) When performing this exercise, you’ll want to ensure your abdominals are engaged the whole time both while stepping up on the BOSU and lowering yourself down.\n2) With the BOSU placed dome side up, place one foot centered on top with the other foot off the BOSU on the ground.\n3) Stand on one leg by loading your bodyweight over top of the foot on the dome of the BOSU by squeezing your glutes, leaning forward, and extending through the front leg until you are standing tall on one leg.\n4) Bring your free leg's knee up in front of you, and counter check your torso's rotation by bringing the opposite arm (opposite from your free leg) across your body. Keep your abdominals drawn in, glutes active, and active leg to minimize wobbles and maintain balance.\n5) Return to the start position by lowering yourself to the ground, sitting and hinging your hips back, and reaching with the free leg to the ground.\n6) Once you’ve completed one side, repeat it on the other.",
